    description: "Found by the 2026-11-24 docstring staleness audit (dev 7e204b35b): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier re-reproduced it on a fixture of its own (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_11242026/review and verify). Corpus impact not measured. _C_DIRECTIVE (discovery.py:657) allows whitespace after '#', so a comment such as '# if you change this, bump PR' or a wrapped '# include this file must set FOO.' is not skipped (L688) and the file is classified other (L690); bitbake.py:147 then drops it. The docstring (L667-670) says '#' comments are skipped. C itself writes '# define' (glibc style), so removing \\s* would break C detection; the decision needs more than one line. r23, v08."  # 3fe6
